### Synapse MinimalApi — Modular Monolith: Cross-Assembly Events
### Demonstrates: two independent modules communicating via a shared event contract.
###   Orders module  — [RequestHandler<>] + source-generated RegisterGroup (emitter)
###   Notifications  — cfg.RegisterEventHandler<>() manual registration (subscriber)
###   Contracts lib  — OrderPlacedEvent (the only shared dependency)
### Run `dotnet run` in examples/MinimalApi, then execute requests top-to-bottom.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5225

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Step 1 — Place an order
# PlaceOrderCommandHandler (Orders module, source-gen) stores the order
# and emits OrderPlacedEvent via IEmitter.
# OrderPlacedNotificationHandler (Notifications module, manual) receives it
# and appends a NotificationEntry to NotificationLog.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [Orders] Place order 1
### Expect: 201 Created with order ID in body
### Observe stdout:
###   📦 [Orders]        "Order <id> placed: 2x Widget"
###   🔔 [Notifications] "Order <id> received: 2x Widget"
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product": "Widget",
  "quantity": 2
}

> {%
    client.test("Order placed", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201 Created");
        client.global.set("orderId1", response.body);
    });
%}

###

### [Orders] Place order 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product": "Gadget",
  "quantity": 5
}

> {%
    client.test("Second order placed", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201 Created");
        client.global.set("orderId2", response.body);
    });
%}

###

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Step 2 — Verify cross-assembly event delivery
# GET /notifications lists all NotificationEntry records that
# OrderPlacedNotificationHandler appended to the NotificationLog singleton.
# Each entry proves the event crossed from the Orders assembly
# to the Notifications assembly via the shared OrderPlacedEvent contract.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [Notifications] List received notifications
### Expect: JSON array with 2 entries (one per order placed above)
### Each entry: { orderId, product, quantity, receivedAt }
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Both order notifications received", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(response.body.length >= 2, "Expected at least 2 notifications");
        const products = response.body.map(n => n.product);
        client.assert(products.includes("Widget"), "Widget notification present");
        client.assert(products.includes("Gadget"), "Gadget notification present");
    });
%}

###

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# What this shows
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  ┌─ MinimalApi.Modules.Orders ──────────────────────────┐
#  │  PlaceOrderCommand → [RequestHandler<>] (source-gen) │
#  │  PlaceOrderCommandHandler: _emitter.EmitAsync(event) │
#  └──────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────┘
#                                     │ OrderPlacedEvent
#                                     │ (from MinimalApi.Modules.Contracts)
#  ┌──────────────────────────────────▼───────────────────┐
#  │  MinimalApi.Modules.Notifications                    │
#  │  OrderPlacedNotificationHandler: IEventHandler<T>    │
#  │  Registered manually:                                │
#  │  cfg.RegisterEventHandler<Handler, OrderPlacedEvent> │
#  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
#  Orders ──────────────────────▶ Contracts
#  Notifications ───────────────▶ Contracts
#  Orders ✗──────────────────────▶ Notifications  (no direct reference)
#
###
